# Terraform state — may contain secrets in plaintext, and belongs in the remote backend.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/

# `.terraform.lock.hcl` is deliberately NOT ignored, matching the other three trees. It is the
# only committed file that names the provider version CI actually ran against: `~> 2.20` in
# required_providers permits every 2.x, and the lock is what makes two people resolve the same
# one. That matters more here than elsewhere — several resources this tree uses are still
# preview in the provider, and a preview resource's schema can change inside a minor release.

# Real variable values. Only the .example files are committed.
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars

# Plan output — can contain sensitive values.
*.tfplan

# Python bytecode.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
